WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:30.170
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS, YOUR PLAYER IS NOT RENDERING THE SUBTITLES PROPERLY. PLEASE REFER TO http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback FOR THE INTENDED PLAYBACK.}

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.130
Strike out!

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.210
All right!

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:54.250
Eight straight wins!

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.800
Nice pitching!

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.430
Now we're five wins ahead of the second placed Rockets!

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:00.550
Victory in the Eastern Division is ours!

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:01.760
Thank you! Thank you!

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.260
Thank you! Thank you!

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.190
"The new catcher, Keane, plays a major part in offense and defense."

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.650
"The leading player in the Bats' advancement," huh?

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:39.170
What are you doing!?

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.220
Put more effort into it! More effort!

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.010
Geez, the old man sure has energy.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.640
I'm tired from all this continuous exercise.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.810
Hey, Sanders!

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:56.530
The thing is, Keane's swelling hasn't gone down from the batting accident yesterday, so I want him to rest.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.360
Can you wear the starting catcher's mask today?

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:04.070
Y-Yes.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:06.120
Hey, Sarge,

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.040
it's been a long time since you've worn the starting catcher's mask.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:11.120
It's not going to be funny if you break our winning streak.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.760
Hey... No. It's a joke. A joke!

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:19.380
Idiot.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.090
You're not funny.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.650
Ball four!

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.440
All right!

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.200
Nice one, Garret!

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.620
All right! We now have the bases loaded with only one out!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.620
Now hitting, number 8: Sanders!

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.120
We're counting on you, Sanders!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.210
H-Hey, is Sarge okay?

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:59.340
He's obviously tense today.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:02.510
He finally got in as a starter, and so far, he hasn't gotten a hit and has two errors.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.800
He hasn't made any good plays yet.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:07.220
It's okay if you go for a sac fly, old man!

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:10.640
Don't try for a homerun, or I won't be able to get the save!

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:18.980
<i>This time for sure...</i>

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:29.620
Out!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:31.330
Out!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.670
Attention please, pitching, number 56:

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:44.170
Goro Shigeno!

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:46.470
Well, one run is enough.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:51.140
Now hitting, number 6: Pedroia!

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.400
<i>Just leave the rest... to me!</i>

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.330
<i>Don't let it get to your head that you got a couple of hits through!</i>

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.130
Ball!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.090
Ball!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:22.760
Ball!

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:32.310
It may be because it's been a while, but it looks like Shigeno and Sanders aren't used to each other.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:38.100
We were all uncertain of Keane's strong and daring lead at first, but as they got used to it,

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:43.610
a catcher like Keane made it easier for the pitchers.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:48.820
They didn't have to think as long as they threw according to the signs.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:53.870
It's a contrast to Sanders' lead, which is conservative and random.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.330
<i>I'll go for the middle!</i>

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.610
Safe!

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:25.990
Shigeno!

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.570
Safe!

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.970
<i>Don't worry about it, Sanders.</i>

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.310
<i>It's not your fault.</i>

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.310
<i>It was my fault for getting hit.</i>

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:12.820
<i>For a second, my body flinched and I tried to tag him with just my glove.</i>

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.660
<i>I got a nice throw to home,</i>

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:22.750
<i>but I chickened out, and not only did I let the first runner score, but also the second.</i>

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.210
<i>Sanders.</i>

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:32.510
<i>When you stay out of the game for a while your instincts weaken, and you can't help making mistakes or hitting easy pop-ups.</i>

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:37.510
<i>But it's the end for a player in the Minors if he loses his fighting spirit.</i>

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:45.520
<i>It may be time now...</i>

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:49.860
Hey, did you hear?

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.070
Hear what?

00:07:52.070 --> 00:07:55.660
Apparently Sanders is going to retire after we come back from this road trip.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.660
A-Are you sure?

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.250
The coach was talking about it, so I'm certain.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:05.460
Well, thanks to Keane, he's been deprived of a job and he made those errors yesterday.

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:09.170
He's also at that age, so he would lose his motivation, I guess.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.130
Hey, Shigeno.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:14.930
What?

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:18.600
Is it true that you're going to quit baseball?

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:21.980
Oh,

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.810
so it's already out.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.270
Why...

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.070
Why aren't you going to stick around to see the Bats win!?

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:32.820
Even if you're a backup now, Keane may get injured or even get promoted!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:33.610
No!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:36.530
Even if you're a backup, you're still a member of the Bats!

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:41.330
Why are you quitting after you said you wanted to see the Bats win and motivated us all!?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:43.330
I have a family.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:49.550
I have a wife and a five-year-old son.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:52.720
Even now, we're living apart, and they're in Boston.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:56.640
My son has never seen me play.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:03.980
I never wanted him to come and see me until I became a Major Leaguer and I could support them with baseball.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:09.610
I can't let him see his old man as an embarrassment, living as a player in the Minors.

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:17.070
But, in the end, I couldn't rise to the Majors and spent my years in the Minors.

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:28.040
I had talked of taking over my wife's family business as a used car dealer, but I was selfish and came here chasing a dream.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:33.510
And because of that, who knows how lonely my son felt.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:37.260
I was never even there for any of his birthdays, and whenever I had time off,

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:43.220
I trained to strengthen myself. I never even took him on a trip.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.230
But...

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.190
that's over now.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:51.270
The time has come for me to return to being a father.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:56.990
It's time to live with my family in a regular and real family life.

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.910
Good luck, Shigeno.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:01.990
I'm wishing for the Bats to win from the bottom of my heart.

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:19.550
Miss Alice.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:21.600
Huh?

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:25.020
You have a phone call from Mr. Shigeno,
who's in the middle of a road trip.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.480
From Shigeno-kun?

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:27.390
About what?

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.350
Apparently it's urgent.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:31.690
Yes?

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:33.150
Oh, it's you.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:34.400
It's me.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:35.940
What? What's the matter?

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:42.240
Did you hear that Sanders is going to make tomorrow's game his last and retire?

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:45.080
Well, yeah.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.540
I am the owner, so I did receive the news.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.170
It can't be helped.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:53.210
This sort of thing happens all the time in this world.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:58.130
It's a shame, but Sarge must have thought long and hard about it and decided.

00:10:58.130 --> 00:11:00.880
It's not something we could talk him out of.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.890
I know.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:04.890
I know that.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:09.060
But there's something I'm not convinced about.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.350
What? "Convinced about"?

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.270
It doesn't matter if it doesn't work out.

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:16.070
Could you help me out?

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:23.450
This is a free fansub.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:23.450
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.750
Hit it, Keane!

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:31.920
Show them a big one!

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:37.300
This is his retirement game, it's the seventh inning, and Sanders hasn't had a turn yet.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.630
It can't be helped.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:44.090
The way this game is going we can't take Keane out for sentimental reasons. We need him,

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.060
but I would like if he got out there as a pinch hitter at least.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:57.610
All right!

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.650
That was great, Keane!

00:11:58.650 --> 00:11:59.940
Nice batting!

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:04.200
All right!

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.820
Now we're tied!

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:11.370
It doesn't look like the batting accident is giving him any problems.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:12.120
Yeah.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.790
That's some rookie.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:22.800
Now hitting, number 3: Morgan!

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:23.380
Go, Morgan!

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:25.220
Follow Keane!

00:12:26.550 --> 00:12:27.430
Boss.

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:32.180
My leg hasn't recovered fully yet, so could I sit?

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.850
Does it still hurt, Keane?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.560
Yes, it does.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:43.110
Then it can't be helped.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.030
Sanders.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.160
You're up at the bottom of this inning!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.070
Get ready!

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.280
Y-Yes!

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:50.580
Hey, are you going in, Sarge?

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.410
We're counting on you, Sarge.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:53.580
Leave it to me!

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.210
Trainer!

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.040
Take a look at Keane's leg!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.420
Hey, Keane.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.510
How much does it hurt?

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.380
Was it when you hit, or was it when you ran?

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.470
No, thank you.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.180
It's all right.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.260
That was a lie.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:09.560
A lie?

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:14.180
To be honest, I didn't really want to go along with this sort of thing,

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:19.020
but Shigeno asked me if I could help out before the game, you see.

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:29.410
<i>So this is the last time I'll be putting on this protector like this...</i>

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:33.540
Out!

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:34.660
Damn it!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.210
That was close. He was so close.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.590
Let's go, Sarge!

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:46.130
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:48.180
<i>I made this decision!</i>

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:52.970
<i>I just need to finish this last game with a win and play without any regrets!</i>

00:13:53.970 --> 00:13:54.890
Play!

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:58.270
<i>All right! Come!</i>

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.570
First!

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.170
Out!

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.000
Out!

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.670
Nice, Sanders!

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:32.680
Now hitting, number 4: Roy!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.430
All right, go for it!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.430
Roy! Get on the base!

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.020
Let's finish this!

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:39.940
Play!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.860
<i>Leave it to me. It's the Sarge's last game.</i>

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:48.650
<i>We can't lose here!</i>

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:52.780
All right!

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:01.830
Out!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:03.960
Damn it!

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.590
Ball four!

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:08.840
All right!

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:12.010
Now hitting, number 8: Sanders!

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:17.100
We're counting on you, Sarge!

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.270
<i>Hit it, old man.</i>

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.020
<i>Hit them one!</i>

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.610
Umpire!

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:28.280
They're changing pitchers.

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:32.610
Attention please, pitching, number 25:

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.160
Gonzalez!

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.300
He sure is popular.

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:49.510
Of course he is.

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:53.140
He was the King of Saves for the Northern League last year after all.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:54.760
The King of Saves?

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:57.010
You don't know Gonzalez?

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:01.640
He has a sharp fastball that goes almost 100mph, and he strikes out the batter 40% of the time.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:07.820
He's been playing in Triple A because of a chronic hip injury, but they say that he may be returning to the Majors soon.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:14.110
Play!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.120
We're counting on you, Sanders!

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:22.790
Strike!

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.420
It's fast...

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.510
<i>So this is a Major League pitch.</i>

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.180
<i>So what about it!?</i>

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.100
Strike two!

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:46.020
<i>I-It's no good...  I can't hit it.</i>

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:53.610
<i>Besides, if I could hit this, I wouldn't have ended my baseball career playing in the Minors.</i>

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.830
Papa!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.120
<i>Jessica! Matthew!</i>

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.130
<i>W-Why are they here!?</i>

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:09.250
<i>Why is my family here at this stadium!?</i>

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.500
Batter!

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.550
Papa!

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.090
Do your best, Papa!

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.020
Strike out!

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:34.360
<i>This is pathetic.</i>

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.570
<i>I let them see such a shameful thing.</i>

00:17:37.160 --> 00:17:39.030
<i>Whose work is this?</i>

00:17:39.030 --> 00:17:43.500
<i>Who told my family that I was going to retire today!?</i>

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.370
Attention please, pitching, number 56:

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.710
Goro Shigeno!

00:17:57.550 --> 00:17:58.640
Thank you.

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:02.430
Finish this, Sarge!

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.600
So it was you?

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.400
Was it you that gave it away to my family?

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.190
Yeah...

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.570
But it was Alice that arranged everything.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.030
That was uncalled for!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:22.160
Who asked you to call my family for my retirement game!?

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:24.620
Did you think you were doing me a favor or something!?

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:29.630
I thought I told you I didn't want my son to see me in disgrace!

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:36.130
As long as I wasn't a Major Leaguer, I wasn't going to let him see his old man's shame till the very end!

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:37.880
And you...

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:39.640
And you just...!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:47.390
Is being a Minor Leaguer that embarrassing?

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:50.810
You're wrong.

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:56.280
My dad was also a baseball player a long time ago.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:19:01.370
He was a player in the Minors for a long time and couldn't rise up to the professionals because of injuries and other things.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.250
Of course Dad wanted me to see him at his best.

00:19:07.200 --> 00:19:11.460
And of course he wanted me to see him gloriously playing an active part in the games.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.380
But to me,

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:22.260
wherever he was, my dad was a hero simply because he was wearing a uniform and playing his best.

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.770
My family is different.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:32.100
My son doesn't think that way.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:35.820
Then why would they come all the way from Boston!?

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:38.610
Besides, if this really is the last time you'll be wearing a uniform,

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:44.070
don't you think your son has the right to see his old man playing his best?

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:50.580
Play!

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.460
<i>He's right.</i>

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:56.670
<i>You're right, Shigeno!</i>

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.590
<i>Why was I trying to act cool?</i>

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:05.800
Strike!

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:09.060
<i>My ten years...</i>

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.770
<i>Was my life in the Minors...</i>

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:17.570
<i>so shameful that I couldn't show it to my son proudly!?</i>

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:26.780
Safe!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:32.080
<i>At least I was serious!</i>

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.080
<i>I was seriously taking it on!</i>

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.760
Knock him down, Wilson!

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:41.970
He's a weak catcher.

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.930
He'll drop the ball again!

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.530
Out!

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.710
All right!

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:26.930
I'm glad you won.

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:28.300
Yeah.

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:31.470
It's all thanks to them.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:33.770
They all played their best to brighten my path.

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:38.980
And what are you going to do after you retire?

00:21:40.150 --> 00:21:41.610
What am I going to do?

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:47.410
I thought we decided way back that I'd work at your father's used car lot.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:53.500
Do you think that position is still open ten years later after you turned it down?

00:21:58.670 --> 00:21:59.630
Papa!

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:02.500
Don't quit, Papa!

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:04.800
I want to see more of your games!

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:08.090
I want to see your team, the Bats, win!

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:13.970
Is that okay?

00:22:13.970 --> 00:22:15.730
Are you both all right with that?

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:20.810
What are you talking about after all these years?

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:23.900
You can always work at the business at any time.

00:22:29.370 --> 00:22:30.530
Papa!

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:32.080
Matthew!

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:16.350
With their new captain, the Seishuu High School baseball club finally enters the summer tournament.

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:19.390
But the team isn't coming together!

00:24:19.680 --> 00:24:21.020
What are you doing, Taiga!?

00:24:22.350 --> 00:24:23.480
Next time, on Major:

00:24:23.480 --> 00:24:25.150
Annoying!

00:24:25.150 --> 00:24:27.610
Run to the stage of your dreams!
